      "created_at": "2019-06-12T13:44:06Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-06-12T13:44:06Z",
      "body": "The map precision level of 2 is at 10km. What would a precision of 4 be? 1? I can see this starting to hinder smaller geographic deployments where the different surveys are more important than the geographic scale. What algo is the randomizer based on? Is it a true random from a physical source (ie Cloudflare) or computer generated? \r\nA goal of the masking of PII would be to have control to scale the range of randomness based on the variance between sources of PII within the map. If 100 sources live within 1.5km, PII randomness can be assigned to a very tight range. If 10 sources are covered over 100km in range, you may need to have a very wide value set for randomization unless that would defeat the purpose of the map, in which case, one should not use a map for this type of data.\r\n",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
